   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-further-maths-shm-q1",
    "gceal-further-maths-shm-q2",
    "gceal-further-maths-shm-q3",
    "gceal-further-maths-shm-q4",
    "gceal-further-maths-shm-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Whether this topic is on the Cameroon GCE Board Further Mathematics syllabus is to be confirmed: it is standard A-Level Further Maths content.",
    "Elastic strings and springs (Hooke's law, elastic potential energy), variable-force work and vertical circles are NOT covered here.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "SHM",
     "md": "A particle performs SHM about $O$ when its acceleration is $x''=-\\omega^2x$ (towards $O$ and proportional to the displacement). Solutions: $x=a\\sin(\\omega t+\\phi)$ or $x=a\\cos(\\omega t+\\phi)$. Amplitude $a$, period $T=\\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega}$, frequency $\\frac1T$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Speed and acceleration",
     "md": "$v^2=\\omega^2(a^2-x^2)$. Maximum speed $a\\omega$ at the centre $x=0$ (where the acceleration is 0). Maximum acceleration $a\\omega^2$ at the ends $x=\\pm a$ (where the speed is 0). Derivation: $v=\\frac{dx}{dt}$ and $x''=v\\frac{dv}{dx}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Springs",
     "md": "A mass $m$ on a spring of stiffness $k$ (Hooke's law $F=kx$) gives $mx''=-kx$, so $\\omega^2=\\frac km$ and $T=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac mk}$. Always identify the equilibrium position as the centre of the motion."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Maximum acceleration is at the ENDS, not at the centre. $\\omega$ is in rad/s, not the frequency. The period does not depend on the amplitude."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "A particle has displacement $x=0.2\\sin3t$ (metres). Find the period, maximum speed and maximum acceleration.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\omega=3$: $T=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}=2.09$ s.",
      "Max speed $a\\omega=0.2\\times3=0.6$ m/s; max acceleration $a\\omega^2=0.2\\times9=1.8$ m/s²."
     ],
     "answer": "$T=2.09$ s; 0.6 m/s; 1.8 m/s²"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "A particle in SHM has amplitude 0.5 m and period 4 s. Find its speed when 0.3 m from the centre.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\omega=\\frac{2\\pi}{4}=\\frac\\pi2$.",
      "$v=\\omega\\sqrt{a^2-x^2}=\\frac\\pi2\\sqrt{0.25-0.09}=\\frac\\pi2\\times0.4=0.628$ m/s."
     ],
     "answer": "0.628 m/s",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": 0,
      "xmax": 3.2,
      "ymin": -0.4,
      "ymax": 0.4,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "0.3*sin(2x)",
        "color": "blue"
       }
      ],
      "points": [],
      "segments": [
       {
        "x1": 0,
        "y1": 0.3,
        "x2": 3.2,
        "y2": 0.3,
        "color": "grey",
        "dash": true,
        "label": "amplitude 0.3"
       }
      ],
      "xlabel": "t (s)",
      "ylabel": "x (m)"
     }
    }
   ],
   "chapter": "gceal-further-maths-applications"
  },
  {
   "id": "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv",
   "title": "Continuous random variables",
   "minutes": 25,
   "programRef": "Cameroon GCE Board — Advanced Level Further Mathematics, Statistics (to be checked)",
   "status": "draft",
   "author": "CastBridge (AI draft)",
   "source": "Original writing following the Cameroonian curriculum; to be reviewed by a teacher",
   "objectives": [
    "Use a probability density function (pdf) and the cumulative distribution function",
    "Calculate mean, variance and median",
    "Find unknown constants"
   ],
   "prerequisites": [],
   "exercises": [
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e07",
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e08",
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e09",
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e10",
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e11",
    "gceal-further-maths-applications-e12"
   ],
   "selfCheck": [
    "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv-q1",
    "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv-q2",
    "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv-q3",
    "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv-q4",
    "gceal-further-maths-continuous-rv-q5"
   ],
   "reviewNotes": [
    "Whether this topic is on the Cameroon GCE Board Further Mathematics syllabus is to be confirmed: it is standard A-Level Further Maths content.",
    "Uniform and exponential distributions as named models, and chi-squared/other tests, are not covered.",
    "Syllabus references, scope and level of difficulty are to be checked against the official text; all facts, formulas and worked examples to be verified by a teacher before release."
   ],
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "pdf",
     "md": "A continuous random variable $X$ has a pdf $f(x)\\geq0$ with $\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f(x)\\,dx=1$ and $P(a<X<b)=\\int_a^bf(x)\\,dx$. Note $P(X=a)=0$, and $f(x)$ may exceed 1 (it is a density, not a probability). The cumulative distribution function is $F(x)=P(X\\leq x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^xf(t)\\,dt$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Mean, variance, median",
     "md": "$E(X)=\\int x\\,f(x)\\,dx$, $E(X^2)=\\int x^2f(x)\\,dx$, $\\text{Var}(X)=E(X^2)-[E(X)]^2$. The median $m$ satisfies $F(m)=\\frac{1}{2}$, i.e. $\\int_{-\\infty}^mf(x)dx=\\frac{1}{2}$. The mode is where $f$ is maximum."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Method",
     "md": "Find unknown constants by $\\int f=1$. Integrate only over the range where $f\\neq0$. For $P(X>c)$ use $1-F(c)$. For the median solve $F(m)=\\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "Integrating over the wrong interval. Forgetting the factor $x$ in $E(X)$ ($\\int xf$, not $\\int f$). Using the mean when asked for the median."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "$f(x)=kx^2$ for $0\\leq x\\leq3$ (0 otherwise). Find $k$, $E(X)$ and $\\text{Var}(X)$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\int_0^3kx^2dx=9k=1$, so $k=\\frac{1}{9}$. $E(X)=\\int_0^3\\frac{x^3}{9}dx=\\frac{81}{36}=2.25$.",
      "$E(X^2)=\\int_0^3\\frac{x^4}{9}dx=\\frac{243}{45}=5.4$; $\\text{Var}=5.4-2.25^2=0.3375$."
     ],
     "answer": "$k=\\frac{1}{9}$; $E(X)=2.25$; $\\text{Var}(X)=0.3375$",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": 0,
      "xmax": 3,
      "ymin": -0.05,
      "ymax": 1.05,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "x^2/9",
        "color": "blue",
        "label": "f(x)"
       }
      ],
      "points": [],
      "segments": [
       {
        "x1": 2.3811,
        "y1": 0,
        "x2": 2.3811,
        "y2": 0.63,
        "color": "red",
        "dash": true,
        "label": "median 2.38"
       }
      ],
      "xlabel": "x"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Find the median of the same distribution.",
     "steps": [
      "$F(m)=\\int_0^m\\frac{x^2}{9}dx=\\frac{m^3}{27}=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
      "$m^3=13.5$, so $m=\\sqrt[3]{13.5}=2.381$."
     ],
     "answer": "$m\\approx2.381$"
    }
   ],
   "chapter": "gceal-further-maths-applications"
  }
